st` with an invalid or unsupported `IO Capability` value (i.e., `0x05` to `0xFF`) must respond with a `Pairing Failed` command, setting the reason code to `Invalid Parameters` (0x0A). This behavior prevents interoperability issues and potential security risks by aborting the pairing process early. Implementations should strictly enforce this rule and log such events for analysis.'}[0m
